      "id": "theverge-2026-08-13-this-is-instagram-8217-s-new-logo",
      "title": "This is Instagram&#8217;s new logo",
      "summary": "It’s certainly… different. | Image: Meta\t\n\nInstagram has unveiled a new wordmark, moving away from the recognizable cursive typeface it's used over the last decade. The updated wordmark is a strange mix of half-cursive half-print that's somehow less legible than its predecessor. Like, that totally says \"Instagzam,\" right?\n\"The wordmark at the top of the app hasn't changed in 10 years, so it was ti",
      "body": "Instagram has unveiled a new wordmark, moving away from the recognizable cursive typeface it’s used over the last decade. The updated wordmark is a strange mix of half-cursive half-print that’s somehow less legible than its predecessor. Like, that totally says “Instagzam,” right?\n“The wordmark at the top of the app hasn’t changed in 10 years, so it was time for a refresh,” Instagram head Adam Mosseri announced on his account. “Cleaner and more modern, with references to the original and the simplicity and craft that’s always made it Instagram.”\nMosseri is seemingly aware that this will be a controversial change, because he also posted it to his Threads account to “see what the hot takes might be.” Plenty of Instagram and Threads commenters have already flagged that the updated version looks like it says “Instagzam,” but the general consensus otherwise is difficult to parse. Some users are mourning the loss of the now iconic cursive wordmark, while other responses — many of which look suspiciously written by bots — are a jumble of positive affirmations and emoji-vomit.\n[Image: Why does “cleaner and more modern” always just mean “we made it look boring and more like everyone else’s branding.” https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/Instagram-wordmark-update.jpg?quality=90&strip=all]\nI don’t personally think it has the same charm, but i’ll leave the rest of you to be the judge of that.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Design",
        "Instagram",
        "Meta",
        "News",
        "Tech"
      ],
      "author": "Jess Weatherbed",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-13T15:00:38.000Z",
