      "id": "hackernews-2026-08-12-i-built-a-browser-native-sysex-librarian-for-80s-90s-synthes",
      "title": "I built a browser-native SysEx librarian for 80s/90s synthesizers",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://bipluk.com/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49279628\nPoints: 8\n# Comments: 5",
      "body": "Back up, organize, and search vintage synth patches directly in your browser.\nalternative you deserve. No driver wall, no app sprawl. One click backs it all.\nhigh-quality interface like the Roland UM-ONE or iConnectivity mio.\n“El iCloud para sintetizadores vintage”\nWhy backups feel stuck in\nSynthesizers are built to last forever, but the digital tools to manage them didn't keep\nA pricing system built for fellow synth heads in the USA\nVintage synthesizers are musical history. Batteries fade, but your patches\ndon't have to. Protect your creative work with simple,\nreliable backups and keep your hardware alive.\nDesktop librarians often cost USD $200+. bipluk+ is just\nonce. Saving over 80% never sounded  better.",
