      "id": "theverge-2026-08-10-costco-8217-s-great-switch-2-console-bundle-includes-over-10",
      "title": "Costco&#8217;s great Switch 2 console bundle includes over $100 in free stuff",
      "summary": "Games look gorgeous on its 7.9-inch screen. | Photo: Brandt Ranj / The Verge\t\n\nThe cost of the Nintendo Switch 2 is going up by $50 on September 1st, 2026, resulting in a $499.99 price tag for just the console. We’re just weeks away, but Costco is offering a fantastic $499.99 bundle for its members that includes a Nintendo Switch 2, a 256GB microSD Express card (usually $59), and a one year subscr",
      "body": "The cost of the Nintendo Switch 2 is going up by $50 on September 1st, 2026, resulting in a $499.99 price tag for just the console. We’re just weeks away, but Costco is offering a fantastic $499.99 bundle for its members that includes a Nintendo Switch 2, a 256GB microSD Express card (usually $59), and a one year subscription to Nintendo Switch Online’s Expansion Pack tier, which normally costs $49.99 per year. That’s over $100 in value, and a great way to kickstart your Switch 2 experience.\n[Product: Nintendo Switch 2 | https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.costco.com%2Fp%2F-%2Fnintendo-switch-2-nso-memory-card-bundle%2F4000435562]\nThe Switch 2 has 256GB of internal storage, so a microSD card is likely something you’ll need eventually for storing more games without having to constantly manage your library. With first-party Nintendo games typically running between 10 and 25GB, and larger third-party games reaching 50GB, a 256GB card should store anywhere from 5-20 additional games.\nThe Switch Online subscription includes a variety of features like cloud saving, online play, plus classic NES, SNES, and Game Boy titles. The Expansion Pack adds games from the GameCube, Game Boy Advance, N64, and Virtual Boy, and includes features for modern games, notably the Switch 2 upgrade packs for The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild and Tears of the Kingdom.&nbsp;\nRead our Nintendo Switch 2 review.",
      "source": "The Verge",
