      "id": "techcrunch-2026-08-08-openai-acquires-presentation-startup-nextslide",
      "title": "OpenAI acquires presentation startup NextSlide",
      "summary": "Founder Ahmed Beshry describes the startup’s product as one “that could turn prompts, notes, documents, or research into a polished, editable presentation.”",
      "body": "12:41 PM PDT · August 8, 2026\nImage Credits:J Studios / Getty Images\nNextSlide recently announced that it’s joining OpenAI, with the presentation startup’s team members now working on ChatGPT.\nThe NextSlide website currently displays a note from founder Ahmed Beshry describing the startup’s product as one “that could turn prompts, notes, documents, or research into a polished, editable presentation.”\nThe ultimate goal, Beshry said, was “to make visual communication more accessible and help more people express their ideas clearly.” So by joining OpenAI, the team will “continue pursuing that same mission: building AI products that help people create, communicate, and turn their ideas into meaningful work.”\nThe financial terms of the deal were not disclosed. In a note on LinkedIn, Beshry said the announcement is coming “a few months late,” as the acquisition took place “earlier this year.”\nBeshry was previously a co-founder at Caper AI, a smart cart/cashier-less checkout startup acquired by Instacart in 2021.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Anthony Ha",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-08T19:41:13.000Z",
